@payments = http://localhost:5103
@orders = http://localhost:5102
@orderId = 1

### Independent simulation (no OrderService required); illustrative standalone order ID
# @name simulatePayment
POST {{payments}}/api/payments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "orderId": 1000000,
  "requestId": "standalone-class-demo-1",
  "amount": 4.50,
  "paymentMethod": "Credit Card"
}

### Replay the identical request above: 200 with the SAME payment ID
### Changed amount/method/key for this order returns 409. No second payment is created.
GET {{payments}}/api/payments/{{simulatePayment.response.body.$.paymentId}}

### Get the payment for a real checkout order (200 or 404)
GET {{payments}}/api/payments/order/{{orderId}}

### Reconcile a saved order after an uncertain outcome; does not create a payment
POST {{orders}}/api/orders/{{orderId}}/payment/reconcile

### Decline demo: restart PaymentService with --Simulation:DeclinePayments true.
### See docs/payment-service.md for the command. Checkout returns 402 and a saved Pending order.
POST {{orders}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerName": "Decline Demo",
  "paymentMethod": "Dining Dollars",
  "items": [{ "menuItemId": 1, "quantity": 1 }]
}

### Missing/invalid inputs (400)
POST {{payments}}/api/payments
Content-Type: application/json

{ "orderId": 1, "requestId": "invalid-demo", "amount": -1, "paymentMethod": "Cash" }
